Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.76,0:00:08.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, how many people using the tokens this day and complain about I'm out of tokens.\N好的，今天有多少人使用词元却抱怨词元用完了。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.74,0:00:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cannot generate image.\N无法生成图像。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.00,0:00:12.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Cannot generate my stack.\N无法生成我的堆栈。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.24,0:00:15.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many people also suffering from slow deployment?\N有多少人也正受制于部署缓慢的问题？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.32,0:00:20.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Get boss, you know, complaining about the revenues delay, all that stuff.\N赶紧去见老板，你知道的，他抱怨收入延迟，还有各种事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.76,0:00:26.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, if that's the case, we are talking about MDC, how we can enable how we can solve those problems.\N好的，如果是这种情况，我们正在讨论 MDC，如何实现，如何解决这些问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.20,0:00:28.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, so Jensen give two missions.\N对，所以黄仁勋提出了两个任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.52,0:00:29.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Simple mission, right?\N简单任务，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.28,0:00:30.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,How hard can that be?\N这能有多难？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.14,0:00:32.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,How we can optimize power for token?\N我们如何优化词元的功耗？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.52,0:00:40.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, as we went through this power crisis, this MDC number one, we are simplified and deliver a more efficient power architect.\N对，经历了这次电力危机后，MDC 排第一，我们简化了设计，交付了更高效的电源架构。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.38,0:00:48.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, cutting back the cutting out the conversion stages, right, and quickly pushing a more simplified compact power design.\N对，减少中间的转换环节，快速推出更简化、紧凑的电源设计方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.64,0:00:55.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And also we are preparing the next generation of the system architect to support the next generation GPUs.\N同时，我们正在为下一代系统架构师做准备，以支持下一代GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.88,0:01:02.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at the same time we try improve the overall efficiency altogether that drives a lower token cost.\N同时，我们努力提升整体效率，从而降低每个词元的成本。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.84,0:01:05.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Secondly, we try to drive the deployment speed.\N其次，我们致力于提升部署速度。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.15,0:01:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, so deployment speed is critical that day one we we embrace AC DC coexistence.\N是的，部署速度至关重要，第一天我们就需要支持交流电与直流电共存。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.08,0:01:18.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, so we can have different user, different stage, but you can deliver different adopt different options.\N是的，我们可以针对不同用户、不同阶段，提供不同的选择方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.48,0:01:20.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And also the footprint can be reduced.\N此外，占地面积也可以缩小。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.80,0:01:26.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Less copper, more integrated system, we can really save the interior space and exterior spaces.\N铜材使用更少，系统集成度更高，我们能真正节省内部和外部空间。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.61,0:01:28.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And lastly, the modular, right?\N最后，是模块化，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.24,0:01:32.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody talk about modular data centers, this is a driver to make it work.\N每个人都在谈论模块化数据中心，这正是推动其实现的关键。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.92,0:01:38.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll turn over to Jared to talk about roadmap.\N接下来我将把时间交给贾里德，由他来介绍路线图。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.28,0:01:42.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this graph here, hopefully everyone's seen a variant of it.\N这张图，希望大家都见过类似的版本。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.93,0:01:43.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh-oh.\N哎呀。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.56,0:01:44.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,There we go.\N就是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.06,0:01:45.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hopefully everyone's seen a variant of this.\N希望大家见过类似的场景。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.82,0:01:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is what's ultimately driving the higher power densities over time.\N这才是推动功率密度随时间不断提升的根本原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.48,0:01:53.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so, we essentially have two things that are going on.\N嗯，我们实际上在同时进行两件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.96,0:01:57.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,One is our GPUs, generation over generation, consume more power,\N一是我们的GPU，每代产品功耗都在增加，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.63,0:02:02.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,but something that's fundamentally different about GPUs is that they get more efficient the more\N但GPU一个根本性的不同之处在于，我们能在相同空间内塞入更多GPU时，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.48,0:02:08.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,GPUs we can pack in the same space uh because we can network them over copper,\N它们的效率会更高，因为我们可以通过铜线互连，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.24,0:02:10.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is gives a better TCO.\N从而带来更低的总体拥有成本。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.00,0:02:16.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so over time, we have power increasing, but then we can very rapidly uh increase power, right?\N所以随着时间推移，功耗在上升，但我们可以非常迅速地提升功耗，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.79,0:02:18.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can very rapidly double.\N它可以迅速翻倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.88,0:02:25.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as power engineers, we don't want to be the bottleneck in the um in all of these AI deployments and all these new systems,\N作为电源工程师，我们不希望成为所有AI部署和新系统中的瓶颈，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.39,0:02:32.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,so we want to get platforms ready so that when uh the chips are are there, they're ready to land.\N所以我们要提前准备好平台，这样当芯片到位时，它们就能立即投入使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.56,0:02:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so for a Gen 1 power rack, we were capable of 145 kW with our 33 kW power shelves.\N因此对于第一代电源机架，我们使用33千瓦的电源货架，实现了145千瓦的功率。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.32,0:02:47.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,For a Gen 2 power system, we are 330 W capable with our 110 kW power shelves.\N对于第二代电源系统，我们使用110千瓦的电源货架，实现了330瓦的功率能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.60,0:02:54.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And for our Gen 3, we've moved to 100 or we are moving 100% liquid-cooled systems.\N而在我们的第三代系统中，我们已转向100%液冷系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.26,0:02:58.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this uh makes it so if we use our DC-to-DC power shelves,\N这样，如果我们使用直流到直流的电源货架，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.90,0:03:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,we can support up to 570 kW in a single rack um with both a 54-V liquid-cooled bus bar as well as liquid-cooled power shelves.\N就能在单个机架中支持高达570千瓦的功率，同时配备54伏液冷母排和液冷电源货架。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.96,0:03:11.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, as those power levels continue to increase,\N随着功率水平持续提升，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.72,0:03:18.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,what we're working on now and what we're not ready to show exactly how it will work is the 800-V native racks, right?\N我们目前正在研发的，也是目前还不准备展示具体实现方式的，就是原生800 VDC机架，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.47,0:03:21.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's that's where we're going long-term.\N这正是我们长期的发展方向。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.24,0:03:28.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so then we're building these systems and we want to harmonize them with the data center.\N因此我们正在构建这些系统，并希望与数据中心实现协同。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.68,0:03:36.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that that's why we're building 800 V is we want we want to both make the rack capable of 1 MW per position,\N正是因为如此，我们才要构建800 VDC系统，以使每个机位都能达到1兆瓦的功率能力，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.32,0:03:41.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,but we also want to make sure that the data center is optimized to what the rack is doing, right?\N同时确保数据中心能针对机架的运行进行优化，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.38,0:03:48.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,That includes energy storage, that includes um efficient distribution, and a simple distribution end to end.\N这包括储能系统、高效的配电，以及端到端的简单配电。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.48,0:03:53.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in order to do that, we we have um uh three different methods.\N为了实现这一点，我们有三种不同的方法。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.61,0:03:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, looking at AC distribution today, we take AC all the way into the rack.\N因此，从当前的交流电配电来看，我们会将交流电一直传输到机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.92,0:04:04.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's where these yellow blocks that we're showing in the diagram, that's where we're putting capacitors,\N这就是图中我们展示的黄色模块所在的位置，我们会在那里安装电容器，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.80,0:04:12.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,electrolytic capacitors for load shaping and dealing with the AI workload fluctuations.\N使用电解电容器来实现负载整形，并应对人工智能工作负载的波动。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.14,0:04:16.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, today that's put into our 110 kW power shelf.\N目前，这些设备被集成到我们的110千瓦电源机架中。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.60,0:04:22.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um then as we move to 800 V DC, that moves into our power rack.\N当我们转向800 VDC时，这些设备将被移至电源机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.25,0:04:26.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we have capacitors local there for energy storage.\N因此，我们会在当地配置电容器用于能量存储。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.25,0:04:29.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um for option B, that's an end-of-row solution.\N对于选项B，这是一种机架末端的解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.88,0:04:34.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And option A and option B, we've we've harmonized into a single solution.\N选项A和选项B已经整合为单一解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.52,0:04:43.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then for option C is where we move to solid-state transformers, and we really go from the gray space all the way to the rack with 800 V DC.\N而选项C则是转向固态变压器，我们真正实现从基础设施区（灰区）到机架全程使用800 VDC。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.37,0:04:47.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we'll we'll walk through these each of these options.\N接下来，我们将逐一介绍这些方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.56,0:04:52.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um So, this is showing uh just DSX today.\N这里展示的是目前的DSX。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.62,0:04:57.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a full super pod with AC input.\N这是一个带有交流输入的完整超级机柜。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.48,0:05:00.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we'll show our power rack.\N然后我们将展示我们的电源机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.72,0:05:06.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this is our 800 V DC MGX power rack, and it takes AC in.\N这是我们 800 VDC MGX 电源机架，它接收交流输入。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.20,0:05:11.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,It outputs 800 V DC, and then with cross cables in the back,\N它输出 800 VDC，然后通过背面的交叉电缆，
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.05,0:05:18.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,it goes into 800 to 54 V DC to DC power shelf, and then powers the 54 V bus bar.\N转换为 800 VDC到 54 V 直流-直流电源机柜，再为 54 V 母排供电。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.28,0:05:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, what this will allow us to do is any rack that's 800 V DC capable, it can then land into an AC data center.\N因此，这使我们能够将任何支持 800 VDC的机柜接入交流数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.68,0:05:41.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, this is showing an updated pod then with that with that power rack, and taking in AC, but then powering up 800 V racks.\N这展示了配备该电源机架的更新机柜，接收交流电，但为 800 VDC机柜供电。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.56,0:05:49.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And presently we can support a one power rack to four compute rack ratio, but that will adjust depending on the power.\N目前我们支持 1 个电源机架对应 4 个计算机柜的比例，但具体比例会根据电力需求调整。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.56,0:06:00.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, for option B, what we've done is we can essentially take that same power rack and integrate it with a remote power panel or a AC PDU.\N对于选项 B，我们所做的就是将相同的电源机架与远程电源面板或交流 PDU 集成。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.18,0:06:08.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so then we take in a large AC feed into the top of the rack and we can then power those same DC to or those same AC\N然后我们将大容量交流电输入机架顶部，即可为这些直流或交流
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.73,0:06:18.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,to 800 V power shelves and then distribute that and treat it just like a remote power panel and power all of the all of the compute racks that way.\N转换为 800 VDC的电源机柜供电，再进行分配，将其当作远程电源面板使用，从而为所有计算机柜供电。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.99,0:06:29.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this is this is something that we would use for like a retrofit situation where you want to retrofit an entire row.\N因此，这适用于需要对整列机柜进行改造的场景。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.64,0:06:38.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, the connector that we've developed, the 125 amp continuous rated connector is rated for 125 amp continuous globally.\N现在，我们开发的这款连接器，额定连续电流为125安培，全球范围内均适用125安培连续电流。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.80,0:06:42.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's uh at 800 V DC.\N这是在800 VDC下实现的。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.36,0:06:50.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we've designed this so that we can basically use it on our power rack and we go from the power rack over to the compute cabinet.\N因此我们设计这款连接器，使其可直接用于我们的电源机架，并从电源机架连接到计算机柜。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.56,0:06:54.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it's also been designed in mind to be used long-term.\N但这款连接器也考虑到了长期使用的需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.24,0:06:56.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when we have 800 V data center,\N因此当我们的数据中心采用800 VDC系统时，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.99,0:07:04.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,it can be hardwired directly into a tap box as a drop cord and plug directly into the back of our DC to DC power shelf.\N它可以直接接入分接箱作为跳线，直接插入我们直流到直流电源架的背面。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.04,0:07:14.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, we're we are moving to the native 800 V racks, but we believe that these DC to DC power shelves and therefore these connectors,\N目前我们正转向原生800 VDC机架，但我们相信这些直流到直流电源架以及相应的连接器，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.14,0:07:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,they'll be used long-term for storage racks, networking racks.\N将长期用于存储机架和网络机架。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.64,0:07:26.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's going to be all the other components in the data center that will need this long-term.\N数据中心中的其他各类组件也将长期需要这种连接器。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.00,0:07:38.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, for that connector and for the the drop cord style tap box, we can we're also our goal is to make this as safe as plugging in an EV, right?\N对于这款连接器以及跳线式分接箱，我们的目标也是让其安全程度达到像插电电动车一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.76,0:07:49.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everyone or it's it's very common, right, to to plug in EV vehicles today for charging and that's all that's all high voltage, right, 400, 800 volts.\N如今，人们普遍为电动车充电，这本身就是高电压操作，电压达到400伏或800 VDC。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.62,0:07:55.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're putting in the same interlocks and safety mechanisms that are already common in that industry.\N我们已引入该行业已普遍采用的互锁和安全机制。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.54,0:08:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the cord by default is off and then it needs to plug in and have a high voltage interlock to ensure the system is safe.\N因此，电缆默认是断开的，需要插上并具备高压互锁，以确保系统安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.04,0:08:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're putting in all of those same mechanisms into the cable and into the the power sources.\N我们正在将所有这些机制都集成到电缆和电源中。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.00,0:08:18.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the next Mike will talk about option C, which is where we actually move to SST powering racks.\N接下来由迈克介绍选项C，也就是我们实际转向使用固态变压器为机架供电的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.16,0:08:18.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.56,0:08:19.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Jared.\N谢谢，贾里德。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.36,0:08:19.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right,\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.67,0:08:24.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,so Jared talking about what A and B for quick adoption but that adoption and also\N所以贾里德在讲A和B选项，便于快速采用，但这种采用以及
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.70,0:08:28.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,for retrofit where option C is where we see it's going to be a North Star,\N在改造场景中，选项C才是我们看到的未来方向。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.53,0:08:28.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.91,0:08:30.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,We try to really accelerate this space.\N我们正努力大力推动这一领域的发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.98,0:08:37.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we show on the screen here is using 34.5 kV as a medium voltage input with RMU loop, right?\N屏幕上展示的是采用34.5千伏作为中压输入，并搭配RMU环路，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.18,0:08:39.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, 600 amp is a standard rating.\N因此，600安培是一个标准额定值。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.35,0:08:44.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that whole loop has 35 35.9 MW of capacity.\N因此，整个环路的容量为35.9兆瓦。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.38,0:08:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, 6 + 1 the N + 1 is what we try to drive here.\N所以，我们这里努力实现的是6+1的N+1冗余。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.32,0:08:53.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you can see we are deploying 5 MW power block integrate with ESS as one module.\N你可以看到，我们正在部署一个5兆瓦的电源模块，并与储能系统集成作为一个单元。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.00,0:08:59.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we have the bottom feed with a auxiliary 5 MW of AC to be reserved.\N然后我们还有底部供电，额外预留5兆瓦的交流电。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.92,0:09:06.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can drive the 6 + 1 compute cluster at 30 MW capacity into the data hall.\N你可以将6+1的计算集群以30兆瓦的容量直接接入数据中心机房。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.30,0:09:09.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you have the reserve loop layer to provide a maintenance access.\N同时，我们还设置了备用环路层，以提供维护接入。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.65,0:09:13.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,This can also be further enhanced as auto transfer scheme, right?\N这还可以进一步升级为自动切换方案，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.88,0:09:21.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you can see this whole block becomes a UPS function with automatic transfer and maintenance access provided.\N所以你可以看到，整个模块现在具备了不间断电源功能，支持自动切换和维护接入。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.09,0:09:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then straight shot single-ended into the data hall compute cluster to support fast deployment fast interconnection.\N然后直接单端接入数据中心计算集群，支持快速部署和快速互联。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.60,0:09:31.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,This day two can be turned into a power container.\N这个单元日可以转变为一个电源集装箱。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.61,0:09:40.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, so we need normal buildings everything can be fully like a parking lot directly plug and play fast deployment parallel to the Okay.\N对，所以我们需要普通建筑，所有设施都能像停车场一样，直接插电即用，实现快速部署，与现场建设并行进行。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.80,0:09:43.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,construction from the factories to the field.\N从工厂到现场的建设。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.36,0:09:47.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that's how we see the futures look like looking like.\N嗯，这就是我们看到的未来模样。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.36,0:09:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, talking SST, right?\N所以，说到固态变压器，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.32,0:09:50.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is just a quick visual.\N这只是一个简短的视觉展示。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.12,0:09:52.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we are promoting outdoor solution as we spoke.\N嗯，正如我们所说，我们正在推广户外解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.67,0:09:54.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it's a 5 MV a target.\N嗯，目标是 5 兆伏安。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.54,0:09:59.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,This has been aligned with Google and Microsoft trends as initial target.\N这个目标已与谷歌和微软的趋势对齐，作为初始目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.33,0:10:07.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh in the same time, right, the ESS direct intertie will link the DCTC content converter inside the container to drive the performance.\N嗯，与此同时，储能系统直接并网将把集装箱内的 DCTC 电源转换器连接起来，以提升性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.66,0:10:13.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and then the catcher could be optional depends on your service uptime and maintenance plan.\N嗯，那么接收端可能是可选的，具体取决于您的服务可用性和维护计划。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.80,0:10:20.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,This one shows exactly how we migrating from AC to DC to be streamlined and then so be more efficient.\N这个图正好展示了我们如何从交流电转向直流电，实现流程简化，从而更加高效。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.12,0:10:27.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, from the seven-layer AC solution and moving to just a four-layer from the grid to the chip, right, with single power conversion.\N对，从七层交流电解决方案，转变为从电网到芯片仅四层，通过单一电源转换实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.85,0:10:33.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that's pretty much where we're going to see the whole thing get very very integrated and compact.\N嗯，这正是我们看到整个系统将变得高度集成和紧凑的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.41,0:10:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, it's not just a voltage change, right?\N嗯，这可不只是电压变化，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.64,0:10:41.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's really drive the simplification, have less conversion stages, and of course smaller footprint.\N这确实能推动简化，减少转换环节，当然还能缩小占地面积。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.41,0:10:46.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's why the containerized module design can be supported.\N这就是为什么可以支持模块化集装箱设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.40,0:10:49.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,This give you a quick overview about how things can get deployed.\N这能让你快速了解部署方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.84,0:10:52.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, so we're showing the RMU to the far left,\N对，我们展示的是最左侧的RMU，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.55,0:10:59.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh where this is the the one of the the the discipline they can design everything on the medium voltage completion.\N这里是中压配电的完整设计，他们可以在此完成所有设计工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.20,0:11:06.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you have the space for the ESS and SST with one OEM control scope for quick interconnections.\N然后你有ESS和SST的空间，采用单一OEM控制范围，实现快速连接。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.55,0:11:11.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where the ESS uh can be sized uh based upon the user definition,\NESS的容量可根据用户定义进行配置，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.53,0:11:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,but of course the power smoothing that'll be a must-have that Jerry will talk about uh in tomorrow's talk in details.\N但当然，功率平滑功能是必不可少的，杰里将在明天的演讲中详细讲解。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.68,0:11:20.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then the power container, like I explained, right?\N然后是电源集装箱，正如我所解释的那样。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.64,0:11:25.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is where you have the SST medium voltage section coming in with SST to deliver 800 DC,\N这里是SST中压部分接入，通过SST输出800 VDC，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.02,0:11:31.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and your DC switchboard will integrate all the power together from the SST output to\N你的直流配电柜将整合SST输出的所有电力，从SST输出端到
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.44,0:11:38.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,the catcher's system and an ESS interconnection and an output feeders directly into the building.\N接收系统的连接、ESS连接以及直接接入建筑的输出馈线。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.28,0:11:40.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Inside building have DCRP, right?\N建筑内有 DCRP，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.20,0:11:41.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,This where things can get fungible.\N这里就是事物变得可互换的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.82,0:11:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Depends on your load requirement, you can design different size RPP.\N根据您的负载需求，可以设计不同尺寸的 RPP。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.52,0:11:52.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And also this DCRP can be different room or adjacent or directly in the same white space as we show.\N而且这个 DCRP 可以位于不同房间、相邻房间，或如我们展示的那样，直接在同一白色空间内。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.40,0:11:57.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the crack units on the side and we are moving towards fully liquid cool solution for the power shelf.\N然后是侧面的裂变单元，我们正朝着电源架的全液冷解决方案迈进。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.28,0:12:05.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the whole thermal uh re thermal management rejection will be fully lowered than 2% as a target.\N因此，整体热管理的散热目标将完全降低至 2% 以下。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.04,0:12:07.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then talk about the ESS.\N接下来谈谈储能系统（ESS）。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.67,0:12:13.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so I'll talk about key functions and tomorrow Jerry has a during our end-to-end performance review,\N嗯，我先讲一下关键功能，明天杰里会在我们端到端性能评审期间进行讲解，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.04,0:12:18.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,we can uh showcase exactly what's the key uh driver in performance of that.\N我们可以准确展示性能的关键驱动因素是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.04,0:12:22.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so you can see this uh ESS is bi-directional device, right?\N嗯，你们可以看到这个 ESS 是一个双向设备，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.38,0:12:25.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,It provides uh number one, it's about full right through, right?\N它提供第一项功能，就是全程贯通，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.03,0:12:33.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is what today best can be done upstream, but it's full right through is more than just connected to the grid under incident or disturbance.\N这是目前上游能做到的最好水平，但全程贯通不仅仅是发生事故或扰动时连接到电网而已。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.79,0:12:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's more important about how you control the IT curve and power quality to meet the compliance to the rack level.\N更重要的是如何控制IT曲线和电能质量，以满足机架级别的合规要求。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.88,0:12:42.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And secondly, the backup power time, right?\N其次，是备用电源的持续时间，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.82,0:12:47.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is where we have friends have BBUs been used a lot to drive that service up time.\N这里，我们的朋友大量使用BBU来提升服务的可用性。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.37,0:12:48.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can treat as a UPS, right?\N你可以把它当作不间断电源，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.04,0:12:51.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where the backup power time can be directly specified.\N可直接指定备用电源时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.96,0:12:53.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And importantly, power smoothing.\N更重要的是，电力平滑。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.39,0:12:59.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a parallel talk uh talk about intelligent power smoothing uh where this is where we uh close\N我们还有一个并行讨论，关于智能电源平滑技术，也就是我们所说的……关闭
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.49,0:13:07.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,to design by NVIDIA directly control uh the SOC signal and it directly control the GPU um uh status,\N由英伟达直接控制片上系统信号，并直接控制GPU状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.79,0:13:08.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.21,0:13:14.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,so it's an active control loop uh to to define and actively tracking the power status.\N因此这是一个主动控制回路，用于定义并实时跟踪电源状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.48,0:13:17.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And lastly, importantly is a load averaging function, right?\N最后，一个重要的功能是负载平均功能，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.43,0:13:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is very critical because we are driving max IOPs.\N这一点至关重要，因为我们正在追求最高的IOPS性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.40,0:13:25.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's important to use ESS to draw this constant load scenario, right?\N使用储能系统来实现这种恒定负载场景很重要，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.69,0:13:31.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So number one, your SST is best perform at a fixed percentage, I say 90%, 95%.\N首先，你的固态变压器在固定百分比下表现最佳，我建议是90%、95%。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.04,0:13:37.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And secondly, you can utilize your SST much, much higher by subscribing most of the GPUs as you can.\N其次，通过尽可能多地订阅GPU，你可以让固态变压器的利用率大幅提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.69,0:13:47.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, so that can be very efficient from the design all the way to the the revenue production using a GPU side.\N对，这样从设计到GPU端的收益生产都能非常高效。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.24,0:13:50.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then most importantly, last part is about the microgrid, right?\N然后最重要的是，最后一部分是关于微电网的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.78,0:13:57.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So as as we design this new architecture, you can start understanding the power container is not just a rectifier.\N所以当我们设计这种新架构时，你就能开始理解电源柜不仅仅是整流器。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.26,0:14:00.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is where you can really find all the sources tied together,\N这里你可以真正将所有电源整合在一起。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.00,0:14:07.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,which today is a 5-MW target, and tomorrow is going to be 10 MW and scalable using SST.\N目前目标是5兆瓦，而明天会达到10兆瓦，并且可通过固态变压器实现扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.44,0:14:11.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, so starting from utility power to the on-prem generation,\N从市电到本地发电，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.17,0:14:14.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,all the way to different renewable energy can tie into to drive\N一直到各种可再生能源都可以接入，以驱动
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.96,0:14:21.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,the optimal uh powers uh sourcing strategy to support environmental and sustainability,\N最优的电源策略，支持环保和可持续发展，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.76,0:14:24.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,and finally, the ESS can be integrated.\N最后，储能系统也可以被整合进来。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.64,0:14:32.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, and this also directly reading exactly what's the current data center uh load requirement from compute, cooling to networking.\N对，这也能直接读取当前数据中心在计算、冷却到网络方面的负载需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.26,0:14:35.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, and then we can we can start training our AI, right?\N对，然后我们就可以开始训练我们的AI了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.75,0:14:47.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you can bring back the tokens, and then feed uh support operation by using this smart intelligent uh controller system as a long-term vision.\N所以你可以重新利用这些词元，然后通过这个智能控制器系统，长期实现支持运营。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.24,0:14:48.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here's the current road map, right?\N这里是当前的路线图，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.76,0:14:56.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,As Charles uh spoke about, we have our current uh power rack sidecar design completed and ready to roll out to be used.\N如查尔斯所说，我们现有的电源机架侧车设计已完成，随时可以推出使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.75,0:15:02.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh very quickly, Q2 next year, uh we have the power center, the end-to-end solution, right?\N很快，明年第二季度，我们将推出整列电源中心，提供端到端解决方案，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.64,0:15:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,To support retrofit or even colos to be fungible targeting at a pod level solution.\N以支持改造项目，甚至实现机柜间的互换性，目标是实现机柜级别的解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.96,0:15:14.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the lastly will be the SST transform rectifiers, where we are targeting Q1 20A, right?\N最后一项将是固态变压器整流器，我们计划在2024年第一季度完成，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.81,0:15:18.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,For the ecosystem to have the full solution ready for deployment.\N为生态系统提供完整的解决方案，随时可部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.80,0:15:20.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and if you look at a journey, right?\N如果你看看整个旅程，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.80,0:15:24.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is not just like, okay, we get solution done and we we call it a day.\N这不仅仅是完成解决方案就结束，然后就宣告大功告成。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.68,0:15:26.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's important to care about grounding protection.\N关注接地保护非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.03,0:15:31.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a separate talk tomorrow with my Microsoft friend Shenyong to discuss exactly\N明天我们将与我的微软朋友沈勇进行一次单独讨论，具体探讨
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.60,0:15:36.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,how the protection should be planned from the operator side or the asset owner side.\N从运营商或资产所有者角度出发，保护方案应如何规划。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.96,0:15:39.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh then we talk about certification, right?\N嗯，然后我们讨论认证，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.07,0:15:46.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are lots of things on the SST side, on the SSCB breaker side, all the way to current limiting device, right?\N在固态变压器方面有很多内容，在 SSCB 断路器方面，一直到限流装置，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.30,0:15:48.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can be certified and proved.\N都可以进行认证和验证。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.06,0:15:49.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um that's very critical, right?\N嗯，这一点非常关键，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.49,0:15:52.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,To make sure all from end to end is fully covered.\N确保从端到端的所有环节都得到完全覆盖。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.29,0:15:56.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And of course, at the same time, we talk about breakers, right?\N当然，与此同时，我们也会讨论断路器，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.05,0:15:59.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um based upon a coordination plan, based upon the full current strategy,\N基于协调计划，基于完整的电流策略，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.60,0:16:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,the end-to-end system, what's the best solution to select the right protection device.\N从端到端的系统来看，选择合适的保护装置的最佳方案是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.92,0:16:08.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um then we talk about connection whips that Jerry directly opened up the spec to\N嗯，然后我们讨论杰里直接开放了规格的连接软线，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.87,0:16:15.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,make sure we're driving this very safe design uh utilizing the EV whips technology with interlock.\N确保我们采用非常安全的设计，利用电动汽车软线技术并配备互锁装置。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.29,0:16:19.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And finally, it's this high-density power conversion where we start from today's 5 MW,\N最后，是在高密度电源转换方面，我们从今天的5兆瓦起步，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.97,0:16:27.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,and shooting for 10 MW for day two and in Britain's uh um microgrid design.\N朝着第二天的10兆瓦迈进，适用于英国的微电网设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.36,0:16:28.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here's the last slide, right?\N这是最后一张幻灯片，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.82,0:16:30.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, like I said, it's a journey.\N所以，正如我所说，这是一段旅程。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.66,0:16:31.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a roadmap.\N这是一张路线图。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.60,0:16:31.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.88,0:16:34.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're driving very quickly on the engineering side, right?\N我们在工程方面正以极快的速度推进，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.30,0:16:41.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, as you know, we're starting from the concept to the architecture, and now we'll define exactly the key components that's required.\N所以，正如你们所知，我们正从概念走向架构，现在我们将明确所需的关键组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.20,0:16:43.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jerry set out the simulation requirement, right?\N杰里明确了仿真需求，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.86,0:16:44.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,\N所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.04,0:16:48.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,we know on the simulation side how things can be compatible with NVIDIA compute and\N我们知道在仿真方面，系统如何与英伟达计算兼容，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.84,0:16:54.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,how we drive the system stability and the the overall right uh simulation uh targets,\N以及如何实现系统稳定性与整体正确的仿真目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.29,0:16:54.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.77,0:16:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,To set the criteria.\N以确定标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.20,0:17:00.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then, moving forward, we're going to get into the prototyping phase, right?\N接下来，我们将进入原型设计阶段，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.42,0:17:06.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,To make sure the system can be validated not just from simulation, but set up from the small scale,\N确保系统不仅可以通过仿真验证，还能从小规模开始搭建，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.35,0:17:12.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,maybe one cell, one one one one power shelf, all the way to a large POC being set up.\N从单个电池单元、单个电源架，一直到大规模的试点项目部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.36,0:17:21.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, everybody from the customer side, from the regulatory side, and then from our team maker side, can all jointly validate the system outcome.\N这样，客户方、监管方以及我们团队的各方都能共同验证系统成果。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.00,0:17:26.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then regulatory will help with compliance and validation.\N然后监管方将协助完成合规性和验证工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.32,0:17:30.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we'll be ready for production readiness, for mass production, and for final deployment.\N我们将为生产准备就绪、大规模生产以及最终部署做好准备。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.88,0:17:33.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And like I said, this is the current option C.\N正如我所说，这是当前的选项 C。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.40,0:17:39.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are moving fast on this one, and like to invite the industry owners to join this journey.\N我们正在快速推进这一项目，也诚挚邀请行业相关方加入这一进程。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.28,0:17:41.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's our presentation.\N这就是我们的演示。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.43,0:17:42.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you guys.\N谢谢大家。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.80,0:17:45.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.48,0:17:47.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Questions for our presenters.\N请问各位演讲者的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.10,0:17:55.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Please line up at the mic.\N请到麦克风前排队。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.88,0:17:59.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey, I'm Sylvia from TE Connectivity.\N大家好，我是泰科电子的西尔维娅。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.54,0:18:01.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have three questions.\N我有三个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.64,0:18:08.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,One, will the 1500 V DC distribution become mainstream in data center?\N第一，1500 V直流配电会成为数据中心的主流吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.53,0:18:12.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if so, what will be the expected timeline?\N如果会，预计什么时候？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.88,0:18:23.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Second question for the SST, and solid state circuit breaker, do you think when will they expect it become mainstream in terms of timeline?\N第二个问题是关于固态变压器和固态断路器，您认为它们何时会成为主流？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.92,0:18:31.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the third is the for the CDU roadmap, do you see what is the next generation 5 megawatt unit will come?\N第三个问题是关于CDU路线图，您能看到下一代5兆瓦单元何时推出吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.76,0:18:32.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, three questions.\N好的，三个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.84,0:18:33.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, quickly.\N好的，快一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.77,0:18:37.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,1500 Let's do one question so that others can also Okay, I'll do it very quickly.\N1500，我们先解决一个问题，这样其他人也能参与。我来快速回答。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.74,0:18:39.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,1500 V DC is not not in the current roadmap.\N1500 V DC 目前不在规划路线图中。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.85,0:18:41.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure which data center do 1500 V DC.\N我不确定 1500 V DC 适用于哪个数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.00,0:18:43.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'd like to hear about it.\N我想听听这方面的内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.13,0:18:45.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,800 V DC has been set because our target is for compute 800 V.\N800 VDC 已经确定，因为我们的目标是计算设备采用 800 VDC。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.97,0:18:49.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're trying to be streamlined for the efficiency.\N我们正努力实现效率的最优化。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.10,0:18:49.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好的？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.48,0:18:51.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I forgot what's your second one.\N我忘了你第二个说的是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.33,0:18:54.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is SST the SST and solid state circuit breaker.\NSST 是固态变压器和固态断路器吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.40,0:18:55.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, SSTB.\N是的，SSTB。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.27,0:18:56.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, go ahead.\N是的，继续说。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.44,0:18:58.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I I just wanted to say for 1500 V,\N嗯，我只是想说关于 1500 V，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.00,0:19:06.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,the the bottleneck is actually the PDB on the compute tray when we go from 800 V direct to a 12 V, right, in the compute tray.\N实际的瓶颈在于计算托盘上的 PDB，当我们从 800 VDC转换到计算托盘内的 12 V 时。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.90,0:19:14.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so if there are any technologies, right, that can give higher density conversion 1500 V direct to 12 in the compute tray.\N因此，如果有任何技术能够实现1500伏直流到12伏的高密度转换，放在计算托盘上，那就再好不过了。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.67,0:19:17.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're interested, but that's that's the challenge, right?\N我们很感兴趣，但这正是挑战所在，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.42,0:19:25.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is we're trying to take the the distribution all the way to the compute tray, and that becomes very difficult at 1500 V.\N我们正试图将配电一直延伸到计算托盘，但在1500伏电压下，这变得非常困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.08,0:19:27.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, SSTB depends on size, 125 amp.\N是的，SSTB的尺寸取决于电流，125安培。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.04,0:19:30.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's getting very available very fast.\N我觉得它正在迅速变得非常普及。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.65,0:19:32.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,We just need certification to be ready.\N我们只需要完成认证即可投入使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.69,0:19:35.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, in the CDU, we are promoting 500 DC.\N对，在CDU中，我们正在推广500伏直流。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.63,0:19:37.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,It should be 800 DC.\N应该是800 VDC。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.12,0:19:37.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has VFD.\N它带有变频器。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.80,0:19:40.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's better to be DC input to drive the efficiency up.\N采用直流输入能更好地提升效率。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.76,0:19:41.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, you can go to next.\N好的，可以进入下一页了。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.00,0:19:43.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.24,0:19:45.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Great presentation, Mike and Jarred.\N演讲非常精彩，迈克和贾里德。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.12,0:19:54.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you please come on comment on what uh standards and codes the industry should drive together in order to make this vision into a reality?\N请问您能否谈谈，行业应共同推动哪些标准和规范，以将这一愿景变为现实？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.00,0:19:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.68,0:20:00.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, I think you mentioned SST, UL 2877, right, is the current placeholder.\N是的，是的，您提到了固态变压器，UL 2877，目前是临时标准。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.99,0:20:06.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'd like to hear from all the industry partners, such as a lot to tell us where's the gap, right?\N我们希望听取所有行业伙伴的意见，告诉我们目前存在哪些差距，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.82,0:20:13.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And secondly, SSCB, right, also UL 91, be specific, has to help to make sure this can be certified.\N第二，SSCB，也就是 UL 91，必须明确具体，以确保能够完成认证。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.85,0:20:19.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I mentioned about current limited approach, right, to make sure that the converter approach,\N我提到了当前对电流限制方法的局限性，以确保转换器方法，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.47,0:20:28.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,DC-DC converter, as well as galvanic isolation, can be approved as a source limiting methods.\N包括直流-直流转换器以及隔离技术，都能被批准作为限流手段。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.08,0:20:30.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi, this is Pranesh from Ampsys.\N你好，我是来自 Ampsys 的普拉内什。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.69,0:20:33.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mike, Sorry, we are like at time.\N迈克，抱歉，我们时间有点紧。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.76,0:20:34.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Quick one.\N呃，快速问一个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.97,0:20:36.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very quick.\N非常快。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.24,0:20:41.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, like I have to follow the process like a way but you are free to I will catch up with you later.\N对不起，我得按流程走，但你可以自由行动，我稍后会找你。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.36,0:20:43.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have about like two two to three minutes.\N我们还有大约两到三分钟。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.60,0:20:45.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you can follow up with the presenters.\N所以，你可以跟进各位演讲者。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.81,0:20:49.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, let's thank our presenters.\N那么，让我们感谢我们的演讲者。
